sparky-stereo-browser (@DEBVERSION@) unstable; urgency=medium

  * The browser no longer dies at start when it is routed to a GPU that is not
    the one Stereo KWin renders on (the Performance profile sends it to the
    discrete GPU): its layers' buffers and hardware decoded pictures carried
    the discrete GPU's modifiers, which the compositor's linux-dmabuf
    feedback does not list, and KWin closed the connection ("importing the
    supplied dmabufs failed"). A frame whose format and modifier the
    compositor does not advertise is copied to shared memory (render
    layers) or drawn into a render layer (decoded pictures); one it
    advertises, as on Mesa, stays zero-copy. The browser still renders on the
    GPU the routing chose.
  * The application menu has 3D Video and 3D Display, the context menu's own
    choices, acting on the page's main video, for pages (YouTube) that take
    the right click for their own menu.
  * WebRender no longer panics "no blob image template" when a transaction
    touches a blob image and deletes it (Mozilla bug 1839001, Glenn Watson).
  * The source states what it is: browser commit a60fdf02ae (Sparky-OS/waterfox,
    branch stereo3d, ORDER 465).

 -- Daniel Ramos (Capitain Jack) <Capitain_Jack@yahoo.com>  @DATE@

